$\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\phi = 0$","input":"The shell that falls from rest at infinity, $\\mu = r_s/2$, for which the mass seen from outside is the rest mass of the dust. In $s = \\sqrt{1 + 8R/r_s}$ its proper time is $c\\tau = -r_s(s - 1)^2(s + 2)/24$, zero where it reaches $R = 0$.","caption":["The plane of $v$ and $r$ ($\\theta = \\pi/2$, $\\phi = 0$) outside the shell, drawn with $v - r$ as the vertical axis so that the ingoing rays, $v$ constant, run at 45°. The shell falls from rest at infinity, crosses $r_s$ at $v = 0$ with $dR/d(c\\tau) = -3/4$, and reaches $r = 0$ at $v = 0.52\\,r_s$, a proper time $5r_s/6c$ later. Inside the shell, $r < R(v)$, space is flat.","Outside $r_s$ the outgoing rays bend away from the horizon, and inside it every future cone points to smaller $r$. From the moment the shell reaches the centre, $r = 0$ is the singularity of Schwarzschild's vacuum, where the Kretschmann scalar $12r_s^2/r^6$ diverges."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"72331bb9956619d8"},"slices":[{"view":"shell","surface":0,"label":"$v - r = -5\\,r_s$","version":"5ce09730969255fe","lines":[[[0.681,0.0714],[1.0,0.0714]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.0714],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"shell","surface":1,"label":"$v - r = -3\\,r_s$","version":"f2c8aceaccd5ffd5","lines":[[[0.4838,0.3571],[1.0,0.3571]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.3571],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"shell","surface":2,"label":"$v - r = -1\\,r_s$","version":"be8ee082775fbc7a","lines":[[[0.25,0.6429],[1.0,0.6429]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.6429],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"shell","surface":3,"label":"$v - r = 1\\,r_s$","version":"3ddddc3f5c1ab45f","lines":[[[0.0,0.9286],[1.0,0.9286]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.9286],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}]}}
